{"cuisine/ancient-roman-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/ancient-roman-cuisine","n":"Ancient Roman cuisine","c":"#a99fb5","crumb":[["Cuisine"]],"sub":"Historical cuisine","intro":[["The cuisine of ancient Rome changed significantly over the duration of the civilization's existence. Dietary habits were affected by the political changes from kingdom to republic to empire, and Roman trading with foreigners along with the empire's enormous expansion exposed Romans to many new foods, provincial culinary habits and cooking methods."],["In the beginning, dietary differences between Roman social classes were not great, but disparities developed with the empire's growth."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ancient-roman-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Roman_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":1,"links":[["Mola salsa","dish/mola-salsa"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Pass the Garum","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pass-the-garum.blogspot.com","note":"Blog by an ancient history graduate recreating Roman recipes as closely as possible to the sources; may no longer be updated.","url":"https://pass-the-garum.blogspot.com/p/about-me.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":3,"rows":[{"name":"Cooking Apicius: Roman Recipes for Today","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Sally Grainger","note":"Classicist and cook Sally Grainger's tested modern versions of recipes from the Roman Apicius collection, from Prospect Books.","url":"https://prospectbooks.co.uk/products-page/current-titles/cooking-apicius","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781903018446"},{"name":"The Classical Cookbook (revised edition)","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Andrew Dalby and Sally Grainger, 2012","note":"Getty Publications book of Greek and Roman recipes adapted from ancient texts by two food historians.","url":"https://shop.getty.edu/products/the-classical-cookbook-revised-edition-978-1606061107","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781606061107"},{"name":"Tasting History: Explore the Past through 4,000 Years of Recipes","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Max Miller, 2023","note":"Book from the Tasting History YouTube series; spans many eras, with several Roman recipes and their sources.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9781982186180","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781982186180"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Farro","ingredient/farro"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."}],"cont":null,"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/1c/Still_life_with_eggs%2C_birds_and_bronze_dishes%2C_Pompeii.jpg/500px-Still_life_with_eggs%2C_birds_and_bronze_dishes%2C_Pompeii.jpg","w":500,"h":296,"by":"Unknown artistUnknown artist","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Still_life_with_eggs%2C_birds_and_bronze_dishes%2C_Pompeii.jpg"}},"ingredient/mashed-potato":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/mashed-potato","n":"Mashed potato","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 7 dishes across 11 cuisines","intro":[["Mashed potato or mashed potatoes (American, Canadian, and Australian English), colloquially known as mash (British English), is a dish made by mashing boiled or steamed potatoes, usually with added milk, butter, salt, and pepper. It is generally served as a side dish to meat or vegetables. Roughly mashed potatoes are sometimes called smashed potatoes. Dehydrated instant mashed potatoes and frozen mashed potatoes are available. Mashed potatoes are an ingredient in other dishes, such as dumplings and gnocchi."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-mashed-potato"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mashed_potato"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":11,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Shepherd's pie","dish/shepherd-s-pie"]]],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Pommes dauphine","dish/pommes-dauphine"]]