"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Grasshopper pie is a no-bake mint-flavored mousse pie with a chocolate crumb crust. Typically light green in color, it is associated with spring, and especially with Easter celebrations in the United States. The pie takes its name from the Grasshopper cocktail."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-grasshopper-pie"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grasshopper_pie"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chow-chow (food)","dish/chow-chow-food"],["Chowder","dish/chowder"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"],["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Cook's Corner","dish/cook-s-corner"],["Crab cake","dish/crab-cake"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dagwood Bumstead","dish/dagwood-bumstead"],["Dagwood sandwich","dish/dagwood-sandwich"],["Deep-dish pizza","dish/deep-dish-pizza"],["Desperation pie","dish/desperation-pie"],["Dirty rice","dish/dirty-rice"],["Donut hole","dish/donut-hole"],["Egg in the basket","dish/egg-in-the-basket"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/4d/Grasshopper_pie_%2814105460720%29.jpg/500px-Grasshopper_pie_%2814105460720%29.jpg","w":500,"h":425,"by":"Julia Payne from Manchester, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grasshopper_pie_(14105460720).jpg"}},"dish/kue-gapit":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kue-gapit","n":"Kue gapit","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kue gapit is an Indonesian kue kering (dry snack) which originates from Cirebon, West Java. Generally made from tapioca flour, its name comes from the cooking process, in which it is grilled between iron molds like a waffle. The snack comes in a variety of shapes and flavors. Though it is a popular souvenir among visitors to Cirebon, residents of the region rarely eat it."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kue-gapit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kue_gapit"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],